{"benchmark": "ifeval", "task_id": "1000", "sample_idx": 23, "model_name": "meta/llama-3.2-3b-instruct", "content": "Raymond III Count of Tripoli was a Prince of the Kingdom of Jerusalem who ruled the County of Tripoli from 1152 to 1187 and was also a claimant to the throne of Jerusalem. He was the son of Raymond II Count of Tripoli and Sibylla of Anjou. In 1152 he married Eschiva of Alpilles. Eschiva was a member of the powerful Alpilsi family.\n\n* **Early Life and Reign **\nRaymond III was born in 1131. He became the Count of Tripoli at the age of 21 after the death of his father in 1152. He was known as a military leader and expanded the County of Tripoli's borders through a series of military campaigns. In 1157 he was captured by the Crusader Kingdom of Jerusalem but was later ransomed.\n\n* **The Third Crusade and Capture by Saladin**\nIn 1187 Raymond III joined the Third Crusade and fought alongside King Baldwin V of Jerusalem and King Amalric I of Jerusalem against Saladin the Sultan of Egypt. During the Siege of Jerusalem Raymond III's forces were defeated and he was captured by Saladin. He was ransomed in 1188 but died the same year at the port of Acre. He died on June 24 1188.\n\n* **Succession and Legacy**\nRaymond III's son Raymond-Roupen went on to rule the County of Tripoli but faced threats from other claimants to the throne. Raymond III's legacy is still remembered in the Middle East today with several towns and cities named after him including the city of Tripoli in Lebanon.", "logprobs": [{"token": "Ray", "logprob": -0.001581966644152999}, {"token": "mond", "logprob": -3.576278118089249e-07}, {"token": " III", "logprob": -0.0001299296854995191}, {"token": " Count", "logprob": -0.1985016018152237}, {"token": " of", "logprob": -3.194758028257638e-05}, {"token": " Trip", "logprob": -0.0002616301644593477}, {"token": "oli", "logprob": -6.01988795096986e-05}, {"token": " was", "logprob": -0.007840453647077084}, {"token": " a", "logprob": -0.36228299140